#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0ba7021-278a-5bfc-8d11-f00a3b63b0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-4x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373528} {:answer/id #uuid "0d863f80-974c-5fd0-9ba0-3d19bf8e3347" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373529} {:answer/id #uuid "22f9d7b5-6e34-51ba-a04a-13901fa9651e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373530} {:answer/id #uuid "31b7712a-30c7-5b25-a8c1-60f541081385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373531} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9220a2-0ad7-50c6-85ed-98e053e99e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532} :answer-field/id #uuid "be7c8072-e10a-55ab-8358-3a565f0a6a95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8fdc31d5-5a66-5e44-b1bd-e6668f2e6e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-104056" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies $y(0)=7.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1-4x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}-4x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({e}^{-x}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=7$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =7 \\\\ -{e}^{-0}+2\\cdot {0}^{2}+C & =7 \\\\ C-1 & =7 \\\\ C & =8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=7$ is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ddf8e77-1f92-52ca-ba0f-d3a0c8aeeddd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373535} {:answer/id #uuid "ddeef60e-4ec8-586c-a724-ac4e52f99051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} {:answer/id #uuid "eaeab17a-7de9-520a-be72-1e945c3a28b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2e}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373537} {:answer/id #uuid "a08229ef-ec6b-54f8-8faf-e2cb18e885e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-3+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373538} {:answer/id #uuid "9474dc52-92f4-5600-a6ca-5868d826ebe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{e{x}^{2}+e}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373539}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} :answer-field/id #uuid "493ad9d4-8aff-5cd3-bb25-1648834bbb25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "52066178-466b-57ba-8963-0e5e66a7bec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104057" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-2x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}-2x){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3}-{1}^{2}+C) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =1 \\\\ C & =e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da866c3-3d7f-5b0b-a810-ac33ce6a862f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡y=(1-x)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375169} {:answer/id #uuid "ff36e7bd-a5e4-5f39-b596-7ff7d49622b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡y=1-2{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375170} {:answer/id #uuid "b064fdd0-a36c-5cee-92e7-9e10247d699e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡y=1-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375171} {:answer/id #uuid "7c31dc57-4c05-53a8-8a8e-94c43bdec15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡y={x}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375172} {:answer/id #uuid "86e781a0-f04d-53d1-ab6b-bd9ecd3bb5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{ln}^{2}⁡y=2{x}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375173}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375171} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c617fb-7a13-5c0b-b392-e9e8047bec0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0ff30466-1dca-57e2-9c20-c453c1fbb920" :question/math-academy-id "q-50219" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{xy}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\n$$ that satisfies $y(0)=e.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{xy}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y} \\\\ \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\text{d}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral in the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$ Then,  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}y}=\\frac{1}{y}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{y}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡y(\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡y+{C}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡y+{C}_{2} & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {ln}^{2}⁡y & =-{x}^{2}+2({C}_{1}-{C}_{2}) \\\\ {ln}^{2}⁡y & =C-{x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2({C}_{1}-{C}_{2})$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=e$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{ln}^{2}⁡e & =C-{0}^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2} & =C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{ln}^{2}⁡y=1-{x}^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80dd6caa-b7e5-5430-9255-ebfcfb0f14b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.002y(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=1\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376016} {:answer/id #uuid "412c8001-8cc2-5d51-ac9a-2a88c39b4385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.002(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=3\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376017} {:answer/id #uuid "af449a69-bb36-51ff-a07f-9f0eb8312294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.002y(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=3\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376018} {:answer/id #uuid "4206d1df-1194-5d9f-bf77-e6035c18064d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.002(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=3\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376019} {:answer/id #uuid "8071c022-f04c-53d7-b274-41d8c2f12f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.002(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=1\\,000" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376020}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376017} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d187d41-b8f4-5db2-bfe5-4298cd8747f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1e431a13-4453-552d-82ca-1466efb78d08" :question/math-academy-id "q-15591" :question/problem "Which of the following initial value problems is an inhibited decay problem?" :question/worked-solution "An inhibited decay initial value problem has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-k(y-a),\\,y(0)={y}_{0}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $y>a$ for all $t>0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited decay problem is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.002(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=3\\,000.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $k=0.002,a=1\\,500,$ and ${y}_{0}=3\\,000.$ Notice that ${y}_{0}>a,$ which is required for inhibited decay. \n\nThe other options do not represent inhibited decay. In particular, the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-0.002(y-1\\,500),\\,y(0)=1\\,000,\n$$\n\ndoes *not* represent inhibited decay model because ${y}_{0}=1\\,000<a=1\\,500.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1101527-9f4f-5301-a5d7-2c4675ea434d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)={e}^{x-3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386898} {:answer/id #uuid "702773f0-c93f-5fdc-8cfc-c4f417f927cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386899} {:answer/id #uuid "db2dc2fe-2a07-5f7b-a570-4e58c725722c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386900} {:answer/id #uuid "09cf98b5-cc32-56bd-a7bc-80017c397c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)={e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386901} {:answer/id #uuid "2723b2b5-87a6-52a2-bd3a-988db461edac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(x)=-{e}^{-x/3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386902}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386900} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5995d24-fede-525d-a40c-73179ae79979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "57dad966-30e8-503a-bfa2-6fa76bd6e7c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119033" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation  ${f}^{′}(x)+3{e}^{-x}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate the derivative term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-3{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) & =-3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3(-{e}^{-x})+C \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdbca57f-16aa-507a-9243-fc5de6668bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4a/4acfee397d2c301aa7d005c8467319969bdfe1a487c284e51024a1851ef8a2e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386905} {:answer/id #uuid "0e615e5e-edb5-5cf5-9379-57b9b7c05caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0e/0e2d84423e017f6d126ef6b997a50d62a7de30f91c24aa64f2525ce4ae33cdd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386906} {:answer/id #uuid "da6e7a98-d892-56d4-877b-036894b8ae90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/14/146aa5565c845f3fbfa66e6c215224236869199844cdbe51f2671c781b1c3705.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386907} {:answer/id #uuid "35676c31-bad6-527d-8d41-0491046fbe5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/3e/3e93190f38d95bd30749fbd1342812c93f593a1d78243f810a3822d5d30eff82.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386908} {:answer/id #uuid "c70ce449-3435-5f49-bbc8-8c5d5d34005e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/55/557708220ba3876b0ae9dbf1d265d11e8d98cf1102ad084d93419543ede35c4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386907} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd2a4ff-6ada-5a27-9174-b3c1a697aa04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "06acaa38-08e2-563c-a31d-7a927dbf62a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119139" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\left(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/cc/cc2ee25a85be3ffdb055853f7665bd53d34003a74b96a14bb947bed39b18e83f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "641c6f0c-3eaf-561b-8356-41cd00f60ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d5/d5f4f2b65878b9c152b5c87e1fac0473f0e76455fc5762ba10f21555d68a60c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386912} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9f2778-f343-5bd4-8b1f-ffa35692fd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/3e/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386913} {:answer/id #uuid "21fe63ba-ca2a-5062-b8c9-c489ae9d0da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a6/a65cbd746c3bb9abe495af168fd7c63e83ecf3d942c5fb478f3d7d312d140b4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386914} {:answer/id #uuid "993af450-e9a5-57fb-a473-cf3bc2a14c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/95/95b3d8fc43562341f93a2bccbcbe36d2a070a2dd6687606175ab5e9580f86e2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386915} {:answer/id #uuid "6f16a9da-248f-5eb6-9d9c-67a9d932876b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0d/0d14e369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca11e9bd38cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386916}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386913} :answer-field/id #uuid "33aa3810-dbfd-5996-9796-56ae579de721" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a05048db-be50-5d0c-8e66-1eb6eda34260" :question/math-academy-id "q-119142" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\left(-\\frac{3(x-1)^{2}}{4}\\right)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\int (x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/e0/e0ff2e64925dcd8bdf298c47815f6e2982fe6091e1ff5dea042f585c67ef1721.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb3b07ff-aef5-5f25-9d62-58beb7b0a9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390973} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c7ff40-2935-56f7-9dc2-fe38a0c6ad84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390974} {:answer/id #uuid "79e7bb7a-8936-5e17-8b1f-480cf0b8051d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390975} {:answer/id #uuid "dc205ce9-1943-5f15-9070-06f16eb5285a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390976} {:answer/id #uuid "155c7953-ebd6-5125-950b-0dbf516f6b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390973} :answer-field/id #uuid "81b19a46-8f9d-50a2-8da7-1578e12a6711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "abd93af3-0e28-559c-8c83-70bb59f81df3" :question/math-academy-id "q-332610" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =5x-y \\\\  & =5(1)-(-1) \\\\  & =5+1 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-x-2y \\\\  & =-1-2(-1) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5e819a-7875-572e-8eb2-bb05664a032d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390980} {:answer/id #uuid "6969347f-013c-5716-b248-5b42f238f060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390981} {:answer/id #uuid "1474c3be-2841-59fd-a69b-176b2d5cd24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390982} {:answer/id #uuid "a6cf9fb9-94c6-575b-a613-48c6446228a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 192\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390983} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad27a47-d093-5c36-a0bf-7265daf0659f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}192 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390983} :answer-field/id #uuid "96925274-8e7d-5159-93dd-aee3f333c8ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "28e64722-99a7-5d4a-b749-394a97d4ce0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332616" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{4t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+16\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 48\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2(4)+0(48) \\\\ 0(4)+4(48)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 192\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20520810-b4a6-5630-bc41-17cb9d317005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390987} {:answer/id #uuid "65e6b3a1-dd4a-5bdb-9ab7-70a3bf5f15eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390988} {:answer/id #uuid "1f15c7b9-5917-506f-9346-531489dc93ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390989} {:answer/id #uuid "def0329a-a2e9-56a8-a107-8950057b96f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390990} {:answer/id #uuid "20bb2938-42f4-5d6f-b5be-8bf12b01f39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-72 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390991}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390988} :answer-field/id #uuid "35839db6-28e1-5c44-9082-b9f7f244356a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "75adf624-a2db-5ea7-93a2-7ef71176d432" :question/math-academy-id "q-332617" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(t)={e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+9\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)+0(-36) \\\\ 0\\cdot \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)+2(-36)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c1207d6-660a-5878-9696-b2a6f678e57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390994} {:answer/id #uuid "c326cefc-3d33-51f6-b6f0-7a69d00ee5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390995} {:answer/id #uuid "bb18a87c-c989-5a99-a62f-c5acf7e387f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390996} {:answer/id #uuid "039ed41b-f17e-574f-b5e7-b148acc75dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390997} {:answer/id #uuid "a58f61bc-6d44-5e5e-b7a6-0aa84d474cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390998}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390995} :answer-field/id #uuid "491749e3-5dfc-5a6a-8c20-a36eb891b6a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "be9877ee-3abb-5c56-bc3e-693bac7c1ef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-332619" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,x(t)={e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+0(6) \\\\ 0\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+1(6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7186fc2-d7d8-5021-9db7-19862e6564d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391001} {:answer/id #uuid "7804d689-9587-56c6-9ec2-fc46413ff481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391002} {:answer/id #uuid "d87b4196-731d-5636-a0e6-fb5cf62cde8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391003} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3186e9-3510-534c-8d19-238c79cedee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391004}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391002} :answer-field/id #uuid "035c96b1-47d3-525c-b3c0-c8ed26f1ce1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db16159-d521-5f88-be7e-27f7a5d92ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391006} {:answer/id #uuid "792cb919-03ee-5f97-8075-ab5dac3f04de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391007} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e8806a-4388-56b5-bdc0-9bc7690028dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391008} {:answer/id #uuid "50858950-c939-535a-92dc-1c535cf70804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391009}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391007} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c9cda5d-a410-57da-87b8-e231cfe1744b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4465eca2-fa42-514f-bf86-62fcd4c733a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-332639" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-3x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=3x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/b6/b6eb04363e97559b51ae43439d965eb19fd7f6acca57916f3159317ceba033ba.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 175921