swer/id #uuid "dc499e49-8bf9-5a9a-aa98-9f42b95ee211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391034} {:answer/id #uuid "57ad1ccc-ffb5-5ea9-98f0-c37832c17e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391035} {:answer/id #uuid "4b78ad5d-e1cb-50b8-9011-e4ea2a270235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391036} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b7e04e-f150-5a0a-b56b-f06f673923b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391037}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391036} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbc060aa-6832-5d50-951d-180706eee4ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391033} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcd393be-3f3a-5d54-b56c-765a247c93c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391039} {:answer/id #uuid "183836bd-4e06-5498-b5e5-9271bdc51698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391040} {:answer/id #uuid "35fcaa94-30df-5985-a1d8-53fde28177f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391041} {:answer/id #uuid "e357655c-0a16-56e0-819e-312ae458e498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391042}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391041} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f45eed4-80c2-5997-82a1-8910e993b93e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ad06d77e-d045-5115-beff-bb5f67391033" :question/math-academy-id "q-332662" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-4x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-4x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=4x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/e1/e1d157e7c921aa6fd2dd5449934baf0258dc5a17fc9f6e6db672a783d59553ca.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20557dcd-5576-575d-9801-a4932bfaed7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/11/11546c8b1c69c2f4f14020f3d7fdbfc322b02e9f6661803783ee54ccd97648e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391098} {:answer/id #uuid "d9629f02-41a5-56bb-be5c-27f85295fb32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/60/60a82fc6876f894285d41742d6ad62d177aa230136b7cdc440b97b392f6c398d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391099} {:answer/id #uuid "47cb6758-4945-5b68-8ca3-e6e504afaff5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/46/460b3691ace4d67d6fd526a8bb9b244a0d2fb55170ed1aac1f2cb6aa849c72c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391100} {:answer/id #uuid "b487d4d5-b824-5bc4-91d1-efcc8f6424ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b2/b24594a5ab369e6952ffb76ded8a48e4186d457d9108e154cb4fd8f96b1749ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391101} {:answer/id #uuid "6550b2ea-565c-5828-9532-04b7406a0cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d1/d1cb187f